    "body": "## BLOCKING CODE REVIEW - Chat 03A, PR #438\n\nReviewed exact HEAD `1fea5b72cc12e08af00fb3c7a2b8795edb25d727` against main `e3c9baeae2ee32e1d9595b1dfe6641cb8f1de97e`, Chat 03 plan and approved Chat 01 contract. Scope and Web/docs SHA parity are correct; `ai-forensics-evidence` passed, but the focused Node test is not part of CI. Independent executable probes of the exact fetched PR module reproduce these blockers:\n\n1. **Two timely commits can incorrectly expire before reveal.** `execute()` checks `command.at >= deadlineAt` before processing `reveal` (around line 253). A committed at 10, B at 20, deadline 100; `reveal` at 100 returns `TIMED_OUT`, phase `expired`, no outcome. The commit deadline must not invalidate a battle whose *both commits* were accepted on time. Define the post-commit reveal/deadline policy explicitly and test it.\n2. **Invalid or unauthenticated command mutates battle at deadline.** Same guard precedes command-type/actor validation: `{type:\"not_a_command\",participantId:\"attacker\",at:100}` on a created battle returns `TIMED_OUT` and appends an event. Reject unsupported commands (and enforce the actor boundary) without lifecycle mutation; only explicitly authorized timeout handling or validated late commands may expire a battle.\n3. **Mechanical DRAW is prematurely treated as FINAL.** The reveal branch sets `phase=\"final\"` and emits `battle.finalized` even when `mechanicalOutcome=\"DRAW\"` (lines 300-306). Chat 01 requires a vote for DRAW, and later for genuinely hand-edited text. Do not implement voting in Chat 03A; preserve a distinct mechanically revealed/not-yet-socially-final state and reserve true finalization for the approved vote/recognition gate. Update public-view reveal logic and tests accordingly.\n4. **Final event ID depends on incidental command history.** `eventId()` encodes the state version (line 61). Independent runs with the same `battleId` and choices produce `same-battle:v3:battle.finalized` versus `same-battle:v4:battle.finalized` when a semantically duplicate commit under another commandId is received. Use a battle-stable terminal event key, e.g. `battleId:final`, with durable uniqueness in the future adapter; keep transition version separately.\n5. **Command ID prototype collisions.** `const prior = currentState.commandReceipts[command.commandId]` (line 237) reads inherited properties. IDs `__proto__`, `constructor` and `toString` on a new battle incorrectly return `COMMAND_ID_REUSE`. Fix own-property access and safe receipt writes/serialization, or strictly validate IDs to rule out reserved names. Add regression tests.\n\nAlso document the trust boundary: `command.at` must be server-authoritative in real PvP, while idempotent retry fingerprints must not accidentally differ merely because a server regenerated that clock value. `seed`, immutable participant snapshots, actual CAS/outbox, and authentication remain open Chat 03 integration requirements; do not silently claim those delivered by this atom.\n\n**Requested next action:** correct these cases IN THE SAME isolated branch/PR; add executable regression tests for each; rerun Node tests, `node --check`, Web/docs mirror parity and exact-HEAD GitHub CI. Keep PR DRAFT, do not merge, do not wire runtime or alter Stage 7.15/UI/economy/NPC. Return the new exact HEAD and results for independent re-review.\n\n**Status: REVIEW BLOCK / NO MERGE / CHAT 03 NOT COMPLETE.**",
