    "body": "## Scope\nImplements the isolated asynchronous tactical_v1 lifecycle requested for Social Combat Chat 03A.\n\n- Versioned two-party battle state with independent immutable commits and reveal gated on both commits.\n- Calls the existing resolver only once during explicit reveal and stores the single mechanical outcome.\n- Deterministic deadline handling at or after the supplied deadline; timeout records the stage and missing participants without assigning a winner.\n- Idempotent command receipts keyed by commandId, altered-content reuse rejection, expected-version checks, and stable event IDs.\n- Internal serialization/recovery and separate participant views that omit both selections and mechanics until reveal.\n- Describes the future atomic persistence adapter/outbox contract without implementing storage.\n- Keeps the module unconnected to active runtime and does not modify legacy battles, Stage 7.15, economy, voting, UI, or NPC behavior.\n\n## Changed files\n- AsyncScene/Web/conflict/tactical-lifecycle.js\n- docs/conflict/tactical-lifecycle.js\n- tools/test_tactical_lifecycle_v1.test.cjs\n\n## Evidence\n- `node tools/test_tactical_lifecycle_v1.test.cjs`: PASS, 120 assertions.\n- `node --check` on both lifecycle files: PASS.\n- Web/docs lifecycle blob SHA matches exactly: `da5cdc5994f8cfba460d2839755d8fceb35b7fc6`.\n- Test blob SHA matches remote candidate: `cb8c6359d10ba9bdfe9d8725e821291f9a101470`.\n- Explicit trailing-whitespace scan: PASS.\n- Exact-head GitHub `ai-forensics-evidence` run `38860730910`: SUCCESS. No lifecycle Node test workflow is configured in GitHub CI; the focused Node test above was run locally against the exact PR blobs.\n\nNo runtime acceptance is claimed. Leave this PR in Draft and do not merge.",
